-- title:
--   Unique edge-chart automorphism from an edge-stabilising g
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$ be irreducible with $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$, and let $K_0$ be a field that is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ have matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$, and let $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ either fix both the homothety class `stdVertex` of the standard lattice $\mathcal O^2$ and its translate by $g_1$, or interchange the two. Fix $n \in \mathbb N$ and write $A_n$ for the quotient of the edge chart ring `chartERing 𝒪 π r` (the localisation away from `edgeQuot.discr 𝒪 π r`) by the ideal generated by the image of $\pi^{n+1}$. The assertion is that there is a unique $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\alpha$ of $A_n$ with the following property: for every commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $xq : A_n \to B$ and every pair of Deligne data $d,d'$ over $B$ relative to $K_0$ and $\pi$ — that is, families of $B$-submodules $\mathrm{line}(M)$ of the base change $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$, indexed by full lattices $M \subset K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, compatible with inclusions and with homothety, and satisfying the stated nondegeneracy at every prime of $B$ — if $d$ lies in the edge chart at the coordinate $xq$, meaning that $d.\mathrm{line}$ at the standard full lattice is the $B$-span of $\bar{xq}(\xi) \otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, that $d.\mathrm{line}$ at $g_1 \cdot (\text{standard lattice})$ is the image under `actBaseChange B g₁` of the span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar{xq}(\eta) \otimes e_1$ (here $\bar{xq}$ denotes $xq$ precomposed with the quotient map, and $\xi,\eta$ are the distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ`, `chartERing.η`), and that `d.InEdgeChart π (g₁ · std) std` holds, and if $d'$ satisfies the same three conditions with $xq$ replaced by $\alpha$ followed by $xq$, then `DeligneDatum.IsPullback B g⁻¹ d d'`, i.e. for every full lattice $M$ one has $d'.\mathrm{line}(M) = (d.\mathrm{line}(g^{-1} \cdot M))$ pulled back along `actBaseChange B g⁻¹ M`.
--
--   This is the transport of the level-$n$ edge chart of the formal Drinfeld upper half-plane under an element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ preserving the standard edge of the Bruhat–Tits tree setwise (end-reversal allowed): such an element acts on the chart ring by a unique $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism, characterised by compatibility with the Deligne-datum description of chart points. It feeds the construction of Mumford-style glueing data at each level, used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky).
